---
import CarpeItDoc from '../../layouts/CarpeItDoc.astro';
import { carpeitOperator } from '../../data/carpeitOperator';

const lastUpdated = '14 October 2026';
const email = carpeitOperator.email;
const privacyMail = `mailto:${email}?subject=${encodeURIComponent('CarpeIt privacy')}`;
---

<CarpeItDoc
  title="CarpeIt — Privacy Policy"
  description="How CarpeIt, the water sports gear rental app, collects, uses and protects your data."
  heading="Privacy Policy"
  lastUpdated={lastUpdated}
>
  <p class="doc-lead">
    CarpeIt connects people who rent water sports gear with the riders, schools and shops who
    lend it. To do that it has to know who you are, what you list and book, and what you say to
    the people you rent with. This page explains exactly what that is, who else handles it, and
    how to get it deleted.
  </p>

  <h2>Who is responsible</h2>
  <p>
    CarpeIt is operated by {carpeitOperator.name} (NIPC {carpeitOperator.nipc}),
    {carpeitOperator.address}, which is the controller of your personal data for the purposes
    of the EU General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR). You can reach us about anything in this
    policy at <a href={privacyMail}>{email}</a>, or by post at the address above.
  </p>
  <p>
    CarpeIt is not required to appoint a Data Protection Officer: it doesn't carry out
    large-scale monitoring of people or large-scale processing of special categories of data.
    Privacy questions are handled directly by the operator at the address above.
  </p>

  <h2>What CarpeIt collects</h2>
  <h3>Your account</h3>
  <p>
    Your email address and a display name, from the way you sign in: Sign in with Apple, or a
    one-time code sent to your email. If you use Sign in with Apple, Apple gives us your name
    and email address, or only Apple's private relay address if you choose to hide your email.
    When you accept the Terms and confirm you are 18 or over, CarpeIt records which version you
    accepted and when.
  </p>
  <h3>Your listings</h3>
  <p>
    What you describe about your gear, its photos, price, deposit and availability, and where it
    can be picked up. Photos are re-encoded on your phone before upload, so the location, time
    and device details a camera records are never sent. Your listing shows an approximate area,
    rounded to about a kilometre. The exact pickup address is shared only with a renter whose
    booking you have accepted.
  </p>
  <h3>Seller details (owners only)</h3>
  <p>
    Before you can lend, you give us your legal name, date of birth (private owners), tax
    identification number (NIF) and the country that issued it, address and phone, and, for
    businesses, your trade register number and a certification that you comply with EU law.
    These are never shown to other users. We need them to identify businesses on the marketplace
    (Digital Services Act, Art. 30) and to report owners' income to the Portuguese Tax
    Authority under Council Directive (EU) 2021/514 (“DAC7”) and Decree-Law 41/2023. If you
    set up a school or shop profile, your business name, type and website are public.
  </p>
  <h3>Your bookings and payments</h3>
  <p>
    The gear, dates, prices, fees, deposits, the Terms version, your safety confirmation at
    checkout, and the status of every booking you make or receive. Card payments are handled by
    Stripe: CarpeIt never sees or stores your card number. CarpeIt keeps a record of each
    payment's amount and status. If you lend gear, Stripe collects the identity and bank details
    it needs to pay you out, under its own terms; Stripe tells us your Stripe account identifier
    and whether your payouts and verification are set up.
  </p>
  <h3>Your conversations and the rental record</h3>
  <p>
    Messages and photos you send to other users; the photo checks at pickup and return,
    including whether each photo was taken with the in-app camera or chosen from your library;
    the other person's agreement or disagreement with a check; problem reports, damage claims
    and their outcome; reviews you write; and reports you file. Handover photos are kept with
    the rental record and are visible to both people on that rental, because they are the
    evidence if something goes wrong.
  </p>
  <h3>Moderation</h3>
  <p>Reports made by you or about you, the decisions taken, and the notices sent.</p>
  <h3>Your device</h3>
  <ul class="doc-list">
    <li><strong>Push token.</strong> If you allow notifications, a push notification token for your device.</li>
    <li><strong>Crash and diagnostic reports.</strong> If the app crashes, freezes or (on iPhone) uses unusual amounts of battery or storage, it uploads a diagnostic report to CarpeIt's servers: what went wrong inside the app, the device model, and your app and operating system versions. On iPhone these come from Apple's MetricKit; on Android, from the app's own crash and “app not responding” reporting. Reports sent while you're signed in are linked to your account. CarpeIt uses them only to find and fix problems, and deletes them after 90 days.</li>
    <li><strong>Approximate location (Android only, optional).</strong> If you allow it in the system permission prompt, the Android app reads your approximate (coarse) location to show gear near you. It is used for that search only and is not stored by CarpeIt. You can say no and search by place instead. The iPhone app doesn't use your device location.</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>What you have to give us, and why</h3>
  <p>
    To create an account you need an email address (or Sign in with Apple), a display name, and
    your acceptance of the Terms and 18+ confirmation: without them we can't run your account or
    prove the contract. To book, you need a payment card with Stripe. To lend, you need Stripe
    payouts and the seller details above, because the law requires them (DAC7 and the Digital
    Services Act) and we can't let you lend without them. Everything else, including
    notifications, location and a profile photo, is optional.
  </p>

  <h2>What CarpeIt does not do</h2>
  <ul class="doc-list">
    <li>No advertising, and no advertising identifiers.</li>
    <li>No tracking across other apps or websites, and no analytics SDKs.</li>
    <li>No selling or renting your data to anyone.</li>
    <li>No access to your contacts, and no precise or background location.</li>
    <li>No decisions about you based solely on automated processing that have legal or similarly significant effects (GDPR Art. 22). Damage claims, reports and account restrictions are decided by a person.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Why it is used</h2>
  <ul class="doc-list">
    <li><strong>To provide the service</strong> (performance of a contract, GDPR Art. 6(1)(b)): your account, listings, bookings, payments, messages, handover records and notifications.</li>
    <li><strong>To meet legal obligations</strong> (Art. 6(1)(c)): identifying business sellers (DSA Art. 30), collecting seller details and reporting owners' income to the Portuguese Tax Authority (DAC7), handling reports and sending moderation notices (DSA Arts. 16–17), and keeping invoices, payment and booking records for accounting and tax purposes.</li>
    <li><strong>Legitimate interests</strong> (Art. 6(1)(f)): keeping the marketplace safe, deciding deposit claims, preventing fraud and abuse, fixing crashes and defects with diagnostic reports, and keeping proof of your Terms acceptance and 18+ confirmation. You can object to these (see Your rights).</li>
    <li><strong>Consent</strong> (Art. 6(1)(a)): push notifications and, on Android, approximate location for “near me” search.</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>Consent, and how to withdraw it</h3>
  <p>
    Notifications and location are asked for through your phone's own permission prompts. You
    can withdraw either at any time in your phone's settings (iPhone: Settings → CarpeIt;
    Android: Settings → Apps → CarpeIt → Permissions or Notifications). Withdrawing doesn't
    affect what was done before, and the rest of the app keeps working.
  </p>

  <h2>Who else handles it</h2>
  <p>CarpeIt relies on a small number of service providers, each processing data on our behalf only to run the service:</p>
  <ul class="doc-list">
    <li><strong>Supabase</strong> hosts CarpeIt's database, file storage and sign-in, in the EU (Ireland).</li>
    <li><strong>Apple</strong>: Sign in with Apple, and push notifications to iPhones through the Apple Push Notification service (APNs).</li>
    <li><strong>Google</strong>: push notifications to Android phones through Firebase Cloud Messaging, and maps and approximate location in the Android app (Google Maps SDK and Google Play services).</li>
    {/* TODO: name the email delivery provider once chosen (e.g. Resend / Postmark / Amazon SES) and add it to the transfers paragraph below. */}
    <li>Our <strong>email delivery provider</strong> sends your sign-in codes and service emails.</li>
    {/* TODO: name the certified invoicing software once chosen (e.g. InvoiceXpress / Moloni). */}
    <li>Our <strong>certified invoicing software</strong> issues invoices for CarpeIt's fee, with the owner's name, NIF and address.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    <strong>Stripe</strong> processes payments, deposits and owner payouts. For identity
    verification (“know your customer”), payouts and fraud prevention on owners' Stripe
    accounts, Stripe acts as an independent controller under
    <a href="https://stripe.com/privacy">Stripe's privacy policy</a>, not on our behalf.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>The Portuguese Tax Authority (AT)</strong> receives the annual DAC7 report about
    owners where DAC7 applies, and may share it with the tax authorities of other EU countries.
    We also disclose data to courts or authorities when the law requires it.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>Push notification previews.</strong> A new-message notification shows its first
    line of text, which passes through Apple's or Google's push service. You can turn previews
    off in your phone's notification settings.
  </p>

  <h3>International transfers</h3>
  <p>
    Some of these providers are based in, or may access data from, the United States: Supabase
    (data hosted in the EU, by a US company), Stripe, Google, Apple and our email delivery
    provider. Where the provider is certified under the EU–US Data Privacy Framework, the
    transfer relies on the European Commission's adequacy decision for it; otherwise, it is
    covered by the Commission's Standard Contractual Clauses. You can ask us for more detail or
    a copy of the relevant safeguards.
  </p>

  <h3>What other users see</h3>
  <p>
    Your display name, rating, listings and reviews, and whether you lend as a private person or
    a business (with the business name), are public. Your messages and rental record are visible
    only to the other person on that rental. Your exact pickup address is shown only once you've
    accepted their booking.
  </p>

  <h2>How long it is kept</h2>
  <p>
    Your account, listings and profile are kept while your account is open. Some records have
    their own limits, and are deleted automatically when they run out:
  </p>
  <ul class="doc-list">
    <li><strong>Messages and handover or claim photos of a rental</strong>: 36 months after the rental ends or is cancelled, the period in which a claim about it can usually still be made.</li>
    <li><strong>Messages about a listing that never became a booking</strong>: 12 months after the last message.</li>
    <li><strong>Reports and moderation notices</strong>: 36 months after the report is made.</li>
    <li><strong>Crash and diagnostic reports</strong>: 90 days, including after you delete your account.</li>
    <li><strong>Bookings, payments, fees and invoices</strong>: 10 years, as Portuguese accounting and tax law requires.</li>
    <li><strong>Seller details used in a DAC7 tax report</strong>: 10 years after the reporting period, as DAC7 requires.</li>
    <li><strong>Your acceptance of the Terms</strong>: as long as the account exists, and afterwards as long as the bookings it relates to.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Deleting your account</h2>
  <p>
    Open CarpeIt, go to Profile, and tap <strong>Delete account</strong>. It happens straight
    away. If you have a rental in progress, finish or cancel it first; requests that nobody has
    answered yet are withdrawn for you. You can also email us from your account's address.
    <a href="/carpeit/delete-account/">Delete your account</a> explains both ways.
  </p>
  <p>
    When you delete your account, your login, email, avatar, listings, listing photos, pickup
    addresses, saved gear, notification tokens, business details and your Sign in with Apple
    authorisation are removed. The text of your messages is replaced with “Message deleted”.
    Records of rentals you took part in, and the payments, reviews, claims and handover photos
    attached to them, are kept for the periods above so the other person still has their record
    and so CarpeIt can meet its legal obligations. Your name on them is replaced with “Deleted
    user”.
  </p>

  <h2>Your rights</h2>
  <p>
    You can ask for a copy of your data (including in a portable, machine-readable format),
    and ask for it to be corrected or deleted, or for its use to be restricted. You can object
    at any time to processing based on legitimate interests, and withdraw consent as described
    above. Email <a href={privacyMail}>{email}</a> from the address on your account, and we'll
    respond within a month. If you're not satisfied, you can complain to the Portuguese data
    protection authority, the <a href="https://www.cnpd.pt">Comissão Nacional de Proteção de Dados (CNPD)</a>,
    or the authority where you live or work.
  </p>

  <h2>This website</h2>
  <p>
    The CarpeIt pages at davidferreira.dev are a static website hosted on GitHub Pages. Like any
    web host, GitHub records technical request data (such as your IP address, browser and the
    page requested) in its server logs to deliver and secure the site; see
    <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement">GitHub's privacy statement</a>.
    The website sets no cookies, uses no analytics or trackers, and loads its fonts from the
    same server rather than from a third party. Email links open your own email app; anything
    you send us is handled as described above.
  </p>

  <h2>Age</h2>
  <p>
    CarpeIt is for adults. You must be 18 or older to use an account, because renting and
    lending involves payments and binding agreements, and you confirm this in the app before
    you start. If we learn that an account belongs to someone under 18, we close it.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
  <p>
    If this policy changes, the new version will be published here with a new date at the top,
    and significant changes will be announced in the app.
  </p>
</CarpeItDoc>
